<h3>My Form</h3>
<p>Use HTML to create a form which submits to the same page. Make your form with 5 inputs that coincide with the  properties in your database. On the page include <code>&lt;bx:dump var="#form#" label="The Form Data" /></code> so you can test the submission of the form.</p>

<bx:output>

    <form action="#cgi.SCRIPT_NAME#?#cgi.QUERY_STRING#" method="post">

        <legend>Books:</legend>

        <p>
            <input type="checkbox" id="dazai" name="dazai">
            <label for="dazai">Osamu Dazai, <i>No Longer Human</i></label>
        </p>
        <p>
            <input type="checkbox" id="greene" name="greene">
            <label for="greene">Joanne Greene, <i>Natural Watercolor Paint Making</i></label>
        </p>
        <p>
            <input type="checkbox" id="martin" name="martin">
            <label for="martin">Molly Martin, <i>The Art of Repair</i></label>
        </p>
        <p>
            <input type="checkbox" id="schwartz" name="schwartz">
            <label for="schwartz">Alvin Schwartz, <i>Scary Stories to Tell in the Dark</i></label>
        </p>
        <p>
            <input type="checkbox" id="shelley" name="shelley">
            <label for="shelley">Mary Shelley, <i>Frankenstein</i></label>
        </p>
        <p>
            <input type="submit" value="Submit">
        </p>

    </form>

    <bx:dump var="#form#" label="The Form Data" />

</bx:output>